# Capture layer

`CaptureService` is an `actor` and *is* the dedicated session queue. It owns the
`AVCaptureSession` and never vends it out, so UI code cannot mutate the session
off-queue. `CameraModel` (`@Observable @MainActor`) is the only type views talk
to.

- All `lockForConfiguration()` work belongs in `CaptureService`, and every lock
  must be balanced with `unlockForConfiguration()` on every early return/throw.
- Pair `beginConfiguration()` with `commitConfiguration()`; never call
  `start/stopRunning()` on the main thread.
- Guard manual controls with `isExposureModeSupported` / `isFocusModeSupported`
  / `isWhiteBalanceModeSupported` / zoom range checks before applying.
- Remove KVO and `NotificationCenter` observers (interruption, runtime error,
  subject-area change) on teardown.
- Start the session only after authorization is confirmed; handle
  `AVCaptureSessionWasInterrupted` and resume.
- Camera Control must degrade gracefully where the hardware is absent.
- Never retain large pixel buffers on the main actor.

Authorization is injected through `CameraAuthorizing` because the simulator has
no camera and tests must never trigger a TCC prompt. Only `.denied` is
resolvable in Settings; `.restricted` and `.noCaptureDevice` must not offer that
affordance.
